  "body": "U4b of #3663. This PR finishes the U4 surface moves that #3931 held back.\n\n## What moved where\n\n- **Properties (saved tool):** the page is a read-only summary (`tool_summary.rs`): type, sizes, holder, spindle rpm, feed, material group, tool number, and the side preview. The button \"Edit in tool library\" opens the tool library window on the tool. The Properties subject does not change. The summary has no Apply.\n- **Shape window:** the holder library picker is removed. The window keeps the Body and Profile tabs (drawn holder, cutter).\n- **Tool library window, Tool tab:** a folded \"Body\" section under \"Holder and stick-out\". It has the stand-in `holder_d` / `holder_len` rows and the body section (Import body…, placement, Pick tip / Pick axis, Apply body, Convert to profile, pieces). It uses the window's own body draft (`ToolEditorView::body`), which `with_library_draft` swaps into `tool_body_ui`. A turning tool shows the Body section and no picker.\n- **Tool library window, Recipes tab:** the rest of the old Cutting data group follows the table: the tool's own spindle rpm and feed, the lathe rows and centre cutting (`tool_settings_grid::cutting_base`).\n\n## Why the three parts are in one PR\n\nThe three parts are one move of the same fields. If the Properties groups go first, the holder and body fields have no editor. If the window gets the Body section first, the same fields have two editors. One PR keeps each field in one editor at each commit (user decision: fewer PRs).\n\n## Kept, and why\n\n- **New-tool form:** Properties keeps the full grid and Add tool. The window has no editor for a tool that is not in the document.\n- **\"Edit tool shape\" on the summary:** the shape window edits through Properties' draft (`tool_ui`), so its door stays beside that draft.\n- **Body tab of the shape window:** it stays. It is the input of \"Convert to profile\" beside the Profile tab, and about 30 tests drive it. The two body drafts are separate, so the two places do not mix. A follow-up can remove it.\n\n## Commands and MCP\n\nNo new command. Each change uses the command that it used before: `ChangeTool`, `ReshapeTool`, `SetToolNumber`, `SetToolBody`, `SetToolBody::library` and the piece commands. No MCP tool is owed. Decision: `docs/decisions/3930-tool-properties-summary.md`.\n\n## Tests\n\nNew pinning tests:\n- `tool_library_assembly::the_body_section_imports_into_the_window_draft_only`\n- `tool_library_assembly::a_turning_tool_has_the_body_section_and_no_holder_pick`\n- `tool_properties::edit_in_tool_library_opens_the_window_on_the_tool`\n\nMoved tests (old → new; the intent is kept):\n- `tool_holder::the_holder_library_is_the_first_thing_the_shape_editor_shows` → `tool_holder::the_holder_library_heads_the_assembly_group_not_the_shape_window`\n- `tool_holder::{apply_holder_lands_the_bt30_er20_and_undo_restores, a_shank_the_holder_cannot_take_is_refused_by_name, the_projection_lands_through_apply_holder_and_undoes, the_picker_lists_the_tts_holders_and_names_the_collar, one_weldon_row_for_each_taper_takes_the_bore_of_the_shank}`: same names, now in the window's assembly group\n- `tool_holder_reference::{a_library_holder_sizes_the_holder_fields_until_its_outline_is_edited, the_profile_tab_names_the_entry_and_the_picker_shows_it, holder_picker_uses_label_left_rows}`: same names, now in the window (Body section, assembly group)\n- `tool_properties::properties_tool_apply_and_undo_use_the_command_history` → `edit_in_tool_library_apply_and_undo_use_the_command_history`\n- `tool_properties::tool_settings_form_a_label_left_grid_in_collapsible_groups` → `tool_settings_form_a_label_left_grid_in_the_window_tabs`\n- `tool_properties::properties_shows_the_settings_and_the_shape_window_holds_the_shape` → `properties_shows_a_summary_and_the_shape_window_holds_the_shape`\n- `tool_properties::tool_page_keeps_apply_and_add_tool_beside_close_without_scrolling` → `tool_page_keeps_its_buttons_and_add_tool_beside_close_without_scrolling`\n- `waterjet_recipe::waterjet_properties_apply_preserves_recipe_refusal` → `waterjet_window_apply_preserves_recipe_refusal_across_a_browser_pick`; the other three waterjet tests keep their names and use the Recipes tab\n- Same names, now drive the window: `tests::tool_settings_edit_live_and_the_shape_editor_follows_its_tool`, `tests::inch_mode_drag_keeps_px_parity_and_types_onto_the_lattice`, `ball_corner_tests::*`, `tap_hand_tests::tap_hand_checkbox_stages_until_apply_and_undo_restores_right`, `tool_cutter_params::the_editors_apply_carries_a_landed_cutter_onto_new_numbers`, `tool_undercut::dovetail_properties_and_editor_edit_flank_angle_without_corner_radius`\n- Layout: `layout_page_tool` (summary anchors), `layout_window_tool_shape` (no picker), `layout_window_tool_editor` (Body section under the group), `structural::tool_editor_structure`\n\nThe `#[test]` count of `crates/ui` goes from 1829 to 1832. No snapshot PNG changes.\n\n## Readings\n\n- Windows (winbuild). Branch head `94012ffed` is trial-merged with `origin/main` `d80dc6944` as `005aec1fe`.\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base origin/main` (`CAMCRAFT_GATE_JOBS=5`): 18 steps, 0 failed, 0 stalled, wall 6.4 min. The steps are the ui build, ui lib (123 s) and 16 ui integration suites. Log: `C:\\camcraft-logs\\gate-3930-94012ffed.log`.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-ui --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean (exit 0).\n- An earlier run of the touched suites on head `1886a08` + 1 fix found one red test (`layout_page_tool`: the button row wraps in the narrow pane). Head `94012ffed` fixes it. The gate above covers that head.\n- Heavy and light lanes: not run. This is a P4 UI PR, and no post or toolpath code changed.\n\n## Screenshots\n\nSeeded document, tool EM-0600-4FL, shell 1600 x 1000.\n\n| | Before (main) | After (this PR) |\n|---|---|---|\n| Properties | ![](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/qsmits/Camcraft/pr-screenshots/pr-3930/before-properties.png) | ![](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/qsmits/Camcraft/pr-screenshots/pr-3930/after-properties.png) |\n| Shape window | ![](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/qsmits/Camcraft/pr-screenshots/pr-3930/before-shape-window.png) | ![](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/qsmits/Camcraft/pr-screenshots/pr-3930/after-shape-window.png) |\n| Tool library window, Tool tab (after: Body section open) | ![](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/qsmits/Camcraft/pr-screenshots/pr-3930/before-library-tool-tab.png) | ![](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/qsmits/Camcraft/pr-screenshots/pr-3930/after-library-tool-tab.png) |\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- A body import through the file dialog in the window. The test uses `import_tool_body_from` with a path.\n- The pixel snapshot `tool_editor_snapshot` (release lane) shows the new shape window at the next cut.\n\nChangelog: The tool Properties page is now a summary with an \"Edit in tool library\" button. The holder pick moved from the tool shape window to the tool library window, and the window's Tool tab has a folded Body section (holder cylinder, body import and placement, pieces).\n\nEffort: high\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nFixes #3930\n",
